From c5bd1d006f4d36ca77d04a91300ac16f1e243a8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 18:25:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] env: keep the aligned keys in stable copies

e2631_env_align_with_baseline() saved values for the non-whitelisted keys
so the exported candidate matches the flash baseline, but it referenced
the key strings through pointers into the first export buffer. The
second export overwrote that buffer, and the restore then called
env_set() with garbage key names: the t92d serial shows "illegal
character '=' in variable name", "Baudrate 0 bps not supported" and
"Error inserting baudrate".

Every tweak record now owns a copy of its key, so a restore can never
depend on a buffer that has since been rewritten. The CLI save path also
joins the parsed block again before writing it, so the exported
candidate stays a valid key=value block instead of the split form used
for the diff.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
---
 board/zte/zxhn-e2631/e2631env.c       | 57 +++++++++--------
 board/zte/zxhn-e2631/e2631env_tweak.h | 89 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 121 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 board/zte/zxhn-e2631/e2631env_tweak.h

